        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Steven Zaillian, Frank Lucas, Richie Roberts\n- Products: American Gangster\n- Places: La Grange, North Carolina, Harlem, the United States, Vietnam War\n- Topics: biographical crime films, drug trafficking, heroin smuggling\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Lucas was born on September 9, 1930.\n- Frank Lucas is an American former drug trafficker who operated in Harlem during the late 1960s and early 1970s.\n- Frank Lucas was a gangster from La Grange, North Carolina.\n- Frank Lucas fictionally inspired the 2007 American biographical crime film American Gangster.\n- American Gangster was directed and produced by Ridley Scott and written by Steven Zaillian.\n- American Gangster depicts Frank Lucas smuggling heroin into the United States on American service planes returning from the Vietnam War.\n- American Gangster depicts Frank Lucas being detained by a task force led by detective Richie Roberts.",
